    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0585" n="479" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg479"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul-General Steinhart to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-09-14T14:41:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">September 14,
                                1906—2.41 p.m</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>President Palma has resolved not to continue at the head of the Government, and
                    is ready to present his resignation, even though the present disturbances should
                    cease at once. The vice-president has resolved not to accept the office. Cabinet
                    ministers have declared that they will previously resign. Under these conditions
                    it is impossible that Congress will meet, for the lack of a proper person to
                    convoke same to designate a new president. The consequences will be absence of
                    legal power, and therefore the prevailing state of anarchy will continue unless
                    the United States Government will adopt the measures necessary to avoid this
                    danger.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhart.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
